---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Meet Malay Association UK, a community keeping Malay culture, food, language and care alive across the UK."
  image="/assets/community-members.jpg"
>
  <div class="design-view design-current">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Our Story</p>
      <h1>From open houses to a growing Malay community.</h1>
      <p>
        MAUK brings people together through the things that feel like home: food,
        language, faith, family, culture and the habit of looking after one another.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section content-grid">
      <article class="story-panel">
        <p>
          Malay Association UK began in the early 2000s with Malay friends and
          families gathering through personal networks. New arrivals, long-standing
          residents and friends of the culture all helped the circle grow.
        </p>
        <p>
          Earlier gatherings often centred around Kelab Melayu, a Malay Club space
          linked to elderly sailors from 1969. After that regular venue was lost in
          2017, the community kept going through open houses, hired halls and a lot
          of gotong-royong energy.
        </p>
      </article>
      <div class="page-image">
        <img src="/assets/family-gathering.jpg" alt="MAUK community members gathered for an outdoor family event" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section">
      <div class="section-heading wide">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Identity</p>
          <h2>Malay roots, UK community, open doors.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          MAUK focuses on Malay culture, language, values, cuisine and welfare. The
          name can sound similar to other groups, so the site is clear about who we
          are and the community work we do.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="stat-row">
        <article class="stat-card">
          <span class="stat-number">1186880</span>
          <p>Registered charity number for Malay Association United Kingdom.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="stat-card">
          <span class="stat-number">CE019955</span>
          <p>Charitable Incorporated Organisation record listed at Companies House.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="stat-card accent">
          <span class="stat-number">1969</span>
          <p>The Kelab Melayu story is part of the spirit MAUK carries forward.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="design-view design-heritage">
    <section class="heritage-about-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Identity</p>
        <h1>Malay roots, held carefully in Britain.</h1>
      </div>
      <aside class="heritage-about-note">
        <p>
          MAUK preserves language, values, cuisine and community memory while
          keeping the doors open to families, friends and future generations.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="heritage-about-ledger" aria-label="MAUK record">
      <div>
        <span>Registered charity</span>
        <strong>1186880</strong>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>CIO record</span>
        <strong>CE019955</strong>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>Community memory</span>
        <strong>Kelab Melayu, 1969</strong>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="heritage-about-grid">
      <figure class="heritage-about-image">
        <img src="/assets/family-gathering.jpg" alt="MAUK community members gathered for an outdoor family event" />
        <figcaption>
          <strong>Community gathering, early MAUK years.</strong>
          Family gatherings, shared meals and formal community work helped keep the association rooted.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="heritage-about-timeline">
        <article>
          <span>Early 2000s</span>
          <h2>A circle becomes an association</h2>
          <p>
            Malay friends and families gathered through personal networks,
            welcoming new arrivals, long-standing residents and friends of the culture.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>After 2017</span>
          <h2>The work continues beyond one venue</h2>
          <p>
            After the regular Kelab Melayu space was lost, the community kept going
            through open houses, hired halls and gotong-royong care.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>Today</span>
          <h2>Heritage, welfare and education together</h2>
          <p>
            The association is clear about who it serves: Malay culture in Britain,
            community welfare and learning that can be passed on.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="design-view design-care">
    <section class="care-about-hero">
      <div class="care-about-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Community Care</p>
        <h1>A volunteer-led charity built around culture, care and service.</h1>
        <p>
          MAUK brings people together through Malay identity, then turns that trust
          into practical support for families, elders and members across the UK.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="care-about-trust" aria-label="Organisation facts">
        <div>
          <span>Charity number</span>
          <strong>1186880</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>CIO number</span>
          <strong>CE019955</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Operating area</span>
          <strong>Across the UK</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="care-about-body">
      <div class="care-about-photo">
        <img src="/assets/volunteers.jpg" alt="MAUK volunteers gathered at a community event" />
      </div>
      <div class="care-about-panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">What Holds It Together</p>
        <h2>Culture creates the trust. Welfare gives that trust a purpose.</h2>
        <p>
          Gatherings, language, food and family networks make it easier to notice
          when someone needs help. That is why social events, education and welfare
          belong in the same association.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="care-about-pillars" aria-label="MAUK work">
      <article>
        <span>Education</span>
        <h2>Pass on Malay language, values and history.</h2>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>Welfare</span>
        <h2>Support elders, families and members facing hardship.</h2>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>Gatherings</span>
        <h2>Keep the community visible, connected and ready to help.</h2>
      </article>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
